    "https://leesmcrae.peopleadmin.com/postings/537": {
      "title": "Assistant Men’s & Women’s Tennis Coach",
      "description": "Lees-McRae College Portal | Assistant Men’s &amp; Women’s Tennis Coach Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Men’s & Women’s Tennis Coach Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Men’s & Women’s Tennis Coach Department MNC Job Description Title: Assistant Men’s & Women’s Tennis Coach Department: Athletics Reports to: Head Men’s & Women’s Tennis Coach Category: Full-time, 12-month Summary/Objective Reporting to the Head Men’s & Women’s Tennis Coach, the Assistant Men’s & Women’s Tennis Coach is responsible for assisting with the goals of guiding and building an elite-level NCAA Division II program. This requires the promotion of academic achievement and character of the student-athlete, fans, and the overall College community. A focus on recruitment and retention of student-athletes, the implementation of a full developmental team program, game knowledge, on-court practice plans, individual player development, generation of net tuition revenue, direction of summer Tennis camps, and meticulous budget management are essential for this position. The Assistant Men’s & Women’s Tennis Coach must abide by the NCAA , Conference Carolinas, and Title IX regulations. Benefits Lees-McRae College offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes Highmark Blue Cross/Blue Shield medical plans with wellness incentives, Aetna dental coverage with orthodontia for children, and a voluntary vision plan for all employees. Life and long-term disability insurance are employer-paid, with optional voluntary life coverage available. Employees can take advantage of flexible spending accounts, a retirement plan with up to 5% employer match after one year, and generous paid time off including vacation, sick, personal, holiday, and college-closed days. Tuition waiver benefits are available for employees and dependents, along with access to a national tuition exchange program. Additional perks include free monthly dining, discounted meal plans, and required direct deposit for payroll. Essential Functions Assisting with overall management of the Tennis program, establishing and adhering to policies, procedures, regulations, and guidelines in compliance with the policies, procedures, regulations, and guidelines of all College, NCAA , State, and Federal Laws. Recruit elite-level prospective student-athletes that will excel within the College framework and make successful progress toward graduation. Monitor academic progress and the retention of students affiliated with the Tennis program, implementing action plans in collaboration with the Faculty Athletic Representative and Burton Center for Student Success. Formulate an effective philosophy to promote the educational welfare and sportsmanship of the student-athlete in alignment with the College’s mission. Assume responsibility for sportsmanship, conduct, and academic progress of all students affiliated with the Tennis program. Plan coaching and practice sessions in accordance with NCAA and Conference Carolinas regulations. Oversee communication with recruits, player evaluations, official visits, and try-outs. Conduct training, development, and supervision for team members. Introduce Tennis techniques and skills through practice sessions and demonstration. Improve level of play and offer opportunities for success as an athlete. Evaluate team members, scout opponents, and address overall team needs. Manage all operational, fiscal, and administrative activities for the Men’s Tennis program. Coordinate and conduct individual workout programs, including conditioning, strength training, and multiple Tennis skill sets. Achieve roster goals through extensive player evaluation and recruitment. Meet net tuition revenue targets by properly awarding athletic scholarships. Oversee a fully, competitive developmental program. Promote the athletic program and Tennis through attending community events, public speaking, fundraising, revenue generation, and marketing. Direct multiple weeks of summer Tennis camp and ID camps throughout the year. Comply with NCAA , conference, and Lees-McRae College regulations and policies. Participate in institutional professional development and training. Display behavior consistent with professional ethics and the Lees-McRae faculty and staff handbook. Special projects and other duties as assigned by the Head Men’s & Women’s Tennis Coach. Competencies Ability to handle information of sensitive and confidential nature in the utmost professional manner. Demonstrate a high level of professionalism, initiative, resourcefulness, and personal accountability. Effective analytical and decision-making skills. Excellent communication (oral and written), organizational, and time management skills. Effective interpersonal skills and ability to work with diverse populations. Ability to recruit and retain elite-level student-athletes. Ability to work independently and prioritize tasks in a deadline-driven environment. Attention to detail and adaptability to a changing environment. Ability to handle stressful situations and adapt as needed. Supervisory Responsibility Direct supervision of one graduate assistant coach, as well as any student assistants or managers. Work Environment Normal office environment in addition to non-traditional environment that includes gymnasiums, weight room, and locker room. Coach can be outside for team activities and extra skill sessions. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work This is a full-time, 12-month position. A flexible work schedule that will include days, evenings, and weekends is required. Work hours vary from 6:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m. or 11:00 a.m. to 8:00 p.m. Monday-Friday, with frequent weekend and evening hours as needed. Travel Extensive travel is typically required for this position to recruit prospective student-athletes and attend away competitions. Occasional travel for conferences, training, or obtaining certifications/licensures may be required. Additional Eligibility Qualifications Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. Three-five years of coaching at the college level or extensive high school coaching experience. Experience with budget development and management. Strong interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills. Self-motivated, proactive, and adaptable with a student-centered approach and strong customer service skills. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree. NCAA Division II coaching background. Certifications: CPR , AED , and First Aid. Physical Demands The employee is occasionally required to sit, climb, balance, stoop, kneel, crouch or crawl. The employee must frequently lift or move up to 50 pounds. Posting Detail Information Posting Number S128P Number of Vacancies 1 Job Open Date Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://leesmcrae.peopleadmin.com/postings/535 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Transcripts Letter of Recommendation Curriculum Vitae Media File Portfolio Teaching Philosophy Office of Human Resources 191 Main Street Banner Elk, NC 28604 rectore@lmc.edu 828.898.8926 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://leesmcrae.peopleadmin.com/postings/206": {
      "title": "Career Opportunities",
      "description": "Lees-McRae College Portal | Adjunct Faculty - School of Business &amp; Management Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Adjunct Faculty - School of Business & Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Adjunct Faculty - School of Business & Management Classification Title Rank Tenure Information Job Description Title: Adjunct Faculty – School of Business & Management Department: Academic Affairs Category: Exempt; Part time; Temporary; Not Benefit Eligible Lees-McRae College is seeking professionals to provide quality learning experiences to traditional and non-traditional students. Adjunct faculty provide instruction in assigned courses on a part-time, as needed basis. Courses may be seated, online, or hybrid format. Some courses are taught at off-campus locations. Adjunct faculty are currently needed for the following disciplines: Marketing / Professional Selling Upper-Level Accounting Operations Management/Supply Chain Data Analytics Essential Functions Utilize current pedagogical methods that foster active and engaged learning. Provide effective quality instruction to students by preparing for each learning experience. Communicating effectively both in verbal and written expression. Follow the course or academic program standards as prescribed by the college. Develop, distribute, and review course syllabi according to the standards provided. Provide supplemental instruction to enhance textbooks and lessons. Use effective evaluation methods to measure student performance. Maintain accurate records (attendance, grades, evaluations, etc.) and submit required reports according to college guidelines. Remain abreast of standards and ongoing developments and practices in the teaching discipline. Competencies Communication Skills Ethical Conduct Teamwork Orientation Thoroughness Supervisory Responsibility This position has no supervisory responsibilities. Work Environment Typical classroom environment. Physical Demands The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work This is a part-time, temporary position. Adjunct appointments do not guarantee course assignments. All adjunct positions are contingent upon enrollment demand. Travel No travel is expected for this position. Required Qualifications Required Education and Experience Master’s degree in related discipline. Related work experiences, professional licensure and certifications, or other demonstrated competencies and achievements that contribute to effective teaching and student learning outcomes. Ability to use technology and online ancillaries. Preferred Qualifications Preferred Education and Experience Earned doctorate/terminal degree in the teaching discipline or a related discipline. Prior college teaching experience. Experience with Brightspace or a similar learning management system. Additional Eligibility Qualifications Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Posting Detail Information Posting Number F011P Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other What is your Philosophy for serving students? (Open Ended Question) Are you authorized to work in the United States? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Transcripts Letter of Recommendation Curriculum Vitae Office of Human Resources 191 Main Street Banner Elk, NC 28604 rectore@lmc.edu 828.898.8926 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
