    "https://leesmcrae.peopleadmin.com/postings/542": {
      "title": "Campus Operations Specialist",
      "description": "Lees-McRae College Portal | Campus Operations Specialist - Shuttle Bus Driver Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus Operations Specialist - Shuttle Bus Driver Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Campus Operations Specialist - Shuttle Bus Driver Department MNC Job Description Title: Campus Operations Specialist- Shuttle Bus Driver Department: Campus Operations Reports to: Director of Campus Operations Category: Non-Exempt Summary/Objective The Campus Operations Specialist / Shuttle Bus Driver is responsible for the safe and timely transportation of students, faculty, and staff across campus. The ideal candidate will demonstrate excellent customer service, route planning, and vehicle maintenance skills, while adhering to all safety and traffic regulations. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Collate and edit transport schedules based on passenger needs. Arrive at designated collection points prior to scheduled departure times. Ensure adherence to passenger limits, both seated and standing. Avoid high-traffic and accident-prone routes when possible. Record and report all major accidents and incidents to the supervisor. Ensure passengers disembark at their correct destinations in a timely manner. Maintain the shuttle bus in a clean, fueled, and roadworthy condition. Observe all relevant traffic and safety laws. Assist with campus mail pickup and delivery. Supervisory Responsibility This position has no supervisory responsibilities. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work This is a full-time position. Typical work hours are Monday through Friday, with a schedule that may vary throughout the year. Occasional evening and weekend work may be required. Travel This position requires regular local travel using a college-owned shuttle vehicle and a clean driving record. Work Environment This role may involve working in various environments, including adverse outdoor conditions such as cold, snow, ice, rain, or heat. Benefits Lees-McRae College offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes Highmark Blue Cross/Blue Shield medical plans with wellness incentives, Aetna dental coverage with orthodontia for children, and a voluntary vision plan for all employees. Life and long-term disability insurance are employer-paid, with optional voluntary life coverage available. Employees can take advantage of flexible spending accounts, a retirement plan with up to 5% employer match after one year, and generous paid time off including vacation, sick, personal, holiday, and college-closed days. Tuition waiver benefits are available for employees and dependents, along with access to a national tuition exchange program. Additional perks include free monthly dining, discounted meal plans, and required direct deposit for payroll. Required Qualifications High School Diploma or equivalent. Valid Driver’s License. One or more years of relevant professional experience. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, particularly Word and Excel. Professional appearance and demeanor with excellent customer service skills. Ability to manage multiple projects, priorities, and deadlines effectively. Preferred Qualifications Experience in an educational or non-profit environment. Strong knowledge of applicable transport and safety codes. First Aid certification is preferred. Excellent route planning and improvisational skills. Friendly and professional demeanor. Physical Demands May be required to stand or walk for extended periods (up to 12 hours) on various surfaces. Must be able to run, climb stairs and ladders, sit, balance, stoop, kneel, crouch, or crawl. Frequently lift or move up to 10 pounds and occasionally lift or move up to 50 pounds. Specific vision abilities required include close vision, distance vision, color vision, peripheral vision, depth perception, and the ability to adjust focus. Posting Detail Information Posting Number S075P Number of Vacancies 1 Job Open Date Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://leesmcrae.peopleadmin.com/postings/308 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Transcripts Letter of Recommendation Curriculum Vitae Media File Portfolio Teaching Philosophy Office of Human Resources 191 Main Street Banner Elk, NC 28604 rectore@lmc.edu 828.898.8926 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
