    "https://leesmcrae.peopleadmin.com/postings/563": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Business Administration",
      "description": "Lees-McRae College Portal | Assistant Professor of Business Administration Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Business Administration Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Job Title Assistant Professor of Business Administration Classification Title Rank Tenure Information Job Description Title:  Assistant Professor of Business Administration School:  School of Business and Management Category:  Full-time faculty position Lees-McRae College is a small, four-year, liberal arts college serving Appalachia and the Southeastern United States. The college is located in the town of Banner Elk in the scenic Blue Ridge Mountains of northwestern North Carolina. Banner Elk is nestled between two popular ski areas and is within a short drive of the Blue Ridge Parkway and the Appalachian Trail. The area is popular to outdoor enthusiasts; skiing, cycling, hiking, climbing, and fly fishing are among the many attractions. The college also owns and maintains the Elk Valley Preserve and Field Station and the May Wildlife Rehabilitation Center. Please visit our website at www.lmc.edu . Benefits Lees-McRae College offers a robust benefits package tailored to support our faculty’s health, financial well-being, and professional growth. Medical coverage is provided through Highmark Blue Cross/Blue Sheild PPO and EPO plans, with wellness incentives through Call to Health that reduce deductibles and other gift cards. Dental and voluntary vision plans offer comprehensive coverage, including orthodontia for children and annual eye exams. Faculty receive employer-paid life and long-term disability insurance with optional voluntary life coverage. Flexible spending accounts are available for medical and dependent care expenses. Retirement benefits include a supplemental plan with up to 5% employer match after one year, with eligibility waivers for prior service. Tuition waiver benefits for undergraduate courses and participation in the Tuition Exchange Program support educational opportunities for faculty and their dependents. All employees are paid via direct deposit. Summary/Objective The School of Business and Management invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Business Administration. This is a full-time, main campus faculty position starting for the academic year 2027-2028. The appointment will begin August 2027. At the time of hire, the successful applicant must have completed a terminal degree (e.g., Ph.D., D.B.A., Ed.D.) in business or a related field. The college is seeking individuals with innovative business and entrepreneurial experiences in teaching. The successful candidate will have expertise in traditional face-to-face teaching and will have expertise in one or more of the following business sub-disciplines: Data Analytics, Operations Management, Entrepreneurship, Marketing, Accounting, Economics. The successful candidate will also teach a PEAK Intensive course on a rotating schedule during the PEAK Intensive academic calendar schedule, which will be paid as a separate contract. Essential Functions Teaching The faculty member will be required to teach 12 credit hours per semester in the discipline and will provide evidence of innovative teaching and curriculum development. The faculty member will teach up to an additional 6 credit hours during the PEAK Intensive academic calendar on a rotating basis. Teaching responsibilities include but are not limited to: classroom management, student assessment, and assessment of student learning. Maintain professional standards of practice in teaching in the classroom. Meet Lees-McRae standards for course syllabi creation and submission, classroom management, use of technology, grade submission, and records management. Advising Support student success through mentoring, tutoring, and advising. Generally, Faculty serve as advisors to students after the first year with the college. Faculty maintain regular office hours to meet with students as outlined in the Faculty Handbook. Scholarship and Professional Development The faculty member is expected to continue their professional development and maintain currency in their field through seminars, classes, or scholarship. Faculty promote and support undergraduate research opportunities. Service Faculty members are expected to serve on committees of the college, school, and Faculty Senate. Faculty are encouraged to participate in service to their community and field. Faculty attend and participate in scheduled faculty/administrative meetings. Other duties as assigned by the Dean of the School of Business and Management The successful candidates will have the capacity for and proven experience to: Create new, innovative, distinctive opportunities for students Provide short- and long-range course and program planning Assist in mentoring/preparing students to reach their career goals Provide leadership and collaboration with the faculty and staff to achieve the vision, mission, goals, and objectives for the Business Administration program, the School of Business and Management, and Lees-McRae College Participate on key committees at the program, school, and college levels Work with college officials and community partners to ensure delivery of high-quality programming Commitment to diversity, inclusion, experiential learning, and community engagement Physical Demands The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. The employee is occasionally required to sit, climb, balance, stoop, kneel, crouch or crawl. The employee must frequently lift or move up to 10 pounds and occasionally lift or move up to 25 pounds. Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision, distance vision, color vision, peripheral vision, depth perception and ability to adjust focus. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work This is a full-time position. Days and hours of work are Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5 p.m. Occasional evening and weekend work may be required as job duties demand. Travel None required. Additional Notes Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. To apply, please complete the application on the Lees-McRae College website and include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching philosophy, unofficial transcripts, and the names of three references with contact information. Any questions regarding the application process, please contact Deborah Lowery at loweryd@lmc.edu Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Required Qualifications A terminal degree in business or a related discipline earned from an accredited institution recognized by the U.S. Department of Education. Appropriate teaching experience at the college level. Expertise in one or more of the following business sub-disciplines: Data Analytics, Operations Management, Entrepreneurship, Marketing, Accounting, Economics Excellent oral and written communication skills. Highly organized and detail-oriented, with the ability to consistently multi-task. Some professional, non-higher education experience. Preferred Qualifications Posting Detail Information Posting Number F052P Open Date Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Transcripts Letter of Recommendation Curriculum Vitae Media File Portfolio Teaching Philosophy Office of Human Resources 191 Main Street Banner Elk, NC 28604 rectore@lmc.edu 828.898.8926 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://leesmcrae.peopleadmin.com/postings/566": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Alumni Relations and Annual Fund",
      "description": "Lees-McRae College Portal | Assistant Director of Alumni Relations and Annual Fund Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Director of Alumni Relations and Annual Fund Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Director of Alumni Relations and Annual Fund Department MNC Job Description Position Title: Assistant Director of Alumni Relations and Annual Fund Department: Alumni Relations and Annual Fund/Institutional Advancement Reports To: Director of Annual Fund and Alumni Relations Lees-McRae is a small, four-year, liberal arts college serving Appalachia and the Southeastern United States. The College is located in the town of Banner Elk in the scenic Blue Ridge Mountains of northwestern North Carolina. Banner Elk is nestled between two popular ski areas and is within a short drive of the Blue Ridge Parkway, and the Appalachian Trail. The area is popular to outdoor enthusiasts: skiing, cycling, hiking, climbing and fly fishing are among the many attractions. The college also owns and maintains the Elk Valley Preserve and Field Station and the May Wildlife Rehabilitation Center. Please visit our website at www.lmc.edu. Benefits Lees-McRae College offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes Highmark Blue Cross/Blue Shield medical plans with wellness incentives, Aetna dental coverage with orthodontia for children, and a voluntary vision plan for all employees. Life and long-term disability insurance are employer-paid, with optional voluntary life coverage available. Employees can take advantage of flexible spending accounts, a retirement plan with up to 5% employer match after one year, and generous paid time off including vacation, sick, personal, holiday, and college-closed days. Tuition waiver benefits are available for employees and dependents, along with access to a national tuition exchange program. Additional perks include free monthly dining, discounted meal plans, and required direct deposit for payroll. Job Summary/Objective The Assistant Director of Alumni Relations and Annual Fund supports the College’s efforts to build meaningful, lifelong relationships with alumni and strengthen broad-based philanthropic support through the Annual Fund, helping build constituent relationships to optimal engagement and higher levels of support. The role provides critical operational, administrative, and constituent support for the Office of Institutional Advancement. This position ensures that advancement activities—including alumni and donor engagement, events, communications, cultivation, stewardship, and data management—are executed accurately, efficiently, and professionally. Working closely with all members of the Advancement team, the Assistant Director serves as a highly organized and dependable partner who anticipates needs, coordinates details, and ensures responsibilities and projects move from planning through successful completion. Essential Functions Coordinates, supports, or leads constituent engagement programs, events, communications, volunteer activities, and annual giving initiatives, as guided by the Director and in collaboration with other members of the Advancement team. Creates positive and consistent experiences for alumni and donors while increasing participation, engagement, and philanthropic support for Lees-McRae College. Assists with the planning, coordination, execution, and follow-up of all Alumni and Advancement events and programs (including event logistics, invitations, registration, guest lists, nametags, materials, décor and set up, vendors, volunteers, and post-event follow-up). Supports the Alumni Board and its ad-hoc committees, ONE Lees-McRae Chapters, and Affinity Groups through meeting preparation, communications, follow-up, and project coordination. Assists in the development and execution of annual giving campaigns, including direct mail, email, social media, and other communication channels. Oversees and leads student philanthropy and engagement programs, including Students Today, Alumni Tomorrow ( STAT ) Club (regular meetings, member training and development, and participation in club meetings and activities), fostering a spirit of generosity and involvement from the freshman year through graduation and promoting student giving and recognition. Develops and implements strategies to engage young alumni (graduates from the last decade) and encourage annual giving. Supports the Parents Council or other parent volunteer groups to strengthen relationships and increase parent participation in giving. Supports employee giving programs, encouraging faculty and staff to support the institution through charitable contributions. Manages the matching gift program, working with donors and their employers to maximize the impact of their contributions. Coordinate reunion giving programs, working with alumni celebrating milestone reunions to encourage special gifts in honor of their class. Works with the Director to identify and cultivate prospective donors, leveraging data and analytics to inform strategies. Collaborates with colleagues in the Advancement team and other university departments to support comprehensive fundraising initiatives. Prepares reports and analyses to evaluate the effectiveness of annual giving programs and make recommendations for improvement. Prepares annual fund donor lists, mailing lists, reports, and other materials to support Advancement activities. Develops content for alumni and donor communications, including newsletters, email campaigns, print materials, and website content. Manages and creates content for the Alumni Association’s social media pages and all regional chapter and affinity group pages, with the approval of the Director. Assists with post-event communications, evaluations, and record keeping Maintains accurate records of alumni and donor interactions and contributions in the university’s CRM . Ensures engagement activities are properly documented in the college’s database. Supports data entry efforts and report building as needed. Assists with the college’s donor engagement, appreciation, and recognition efforts, ensuring donors receive timely and meaningful acknowledgment of their support. Represents the college at events and activities, both on and off-campus, to promote the college’s interests and achieve its goals. Performs other duties as assigned. Competencies Written and verbal communication proficiency Proficient in MS Word/365 suite, social media channels, and CRM management Acts with integrity in all work Confidentiality Highly organized and exceptionally detail-oriented Relentlessly focused on follow-through Anticipatory of role’s and division’s needs Takes ownership of getting work completed with excellence Professional in demeanor and appearance Excellent customer service Responsive, warm, and welcoming to all Positive, can-do approach Time management Problem solving/analysis Teamwork orientation, but comfortable working independently Supervisory Responsibility Supervision of students and volunteers Work Environment Environment varies by project and need. Typical office environment for daily work Special event venues and environments will vary both on and off campus. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work This is a full-time, exempt position. Typical days and hours of work are Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m., but schedule regularly requires evening and weekend work. Travel This position requires occasional travel, generally less than 30%, for alumni events, donor and constituent activities, professional development, and other College-related activities. At-Will Employment Disclaimer This job description is not intended to be a contract of employment. Employment with the Company is at-will, which means that either the employee or the Company may terminate the employment relationship at any time, with or without cause or notice, subject to applicable law. The Company reserves the right to revise, modify, or change job duties and responsibilities as business needs dictate. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Minimum of one year’s experience in alumni relations, advancement, non profit or higher education operations Experience in communications, event management, sales or a related field may be considered in lieu of field-specific experience. Preferred Qualifications Degree in public relations, communications/English, or marketing Experience managing volunteers Experience managing Ellucian products Content development experience Data visualization experience Physical Demands Ability to sit and work at a computer for extended periods. Ability to communicate effectively in person, by telephone, and through electronic communication. Ability to independently and routinely move throughout campus and travel to event locations. Ability to lift and carry materials weighing up to 50 pounds. Ability to assist with event set-up, breakdown, and movement of event materials as needed. Ability to work evenings and weekend and to perform the essential functions of the position with or without reasonable accommodation. Posting Detail Information Posting Number S133P Number of Vacancies 1 Job Open Date Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://leesmcrae.peopleadmin.com/postings/564 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Transcripts Letter of Recommendation Curriculum Vitae Media File Portfolio Office of Human Resources 191 Main Street Banner Elk, NC 28604 rectore@lmc.edu 828.898.8926 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://leesmcrae.peopleadmin.com/postings/571": {
      "title": "Assistant Alpine Ski/Snowboard Coach",
      "description": "Lees-McRae College Portal | Assistant Alpine Ski/Snowboard Coach Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Alpine Ski/Snowboard Coach Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Alpine Ski/Snowboard Coach Department MNC Job Description Title: Assistant Alpine Ski Coach Department: Athletics Reports to: Head Ski and Snowboard Coach Category: Part-time, 12-month Summary/Objective Reporting to the Head Ski and Snowboard Coach, the Assistant Alpine Ski Coach is responsible for assisting the head coach in meeting the goals of guiding and building an elite-level program. This requires the promotion of academic achievement and character of the student-athlete, fans, and the overall College community. The Assistant Alpine Ski Coach will have a strong background in alpine skiing and several years of race coaching. The coach is responsible for recruiting, budget management, athlete development, and all aspects pertaining to the rules of Lees-McRae College and the United States Collegiate Ski & Snowboard Association ( USCSA ). A focus on recruitment and retention of student-athletes, growing and maintaining rosters, competition preparation, generation of net tuition revenue, and meticulous budget management are essential for this position. Essential Functions Create training/practice schedules. Ski while carrying up to 50lbs. Coordinate travel/competition logistics during the season. Work in an outdoor alpine environment during adverse conditions. Travel with the team for competitions. Effectively manage an annual budget. Participate in fundraising/community events. Engage with student-athletes and follow up on academic progress. Assist the Head Coach in the day-to-day operations which includes preparation, organization and implementation of effective practice schedules, off-season programs, and in-season competition. Evaluation and recruitment of elite prospective student-athletes. Monitoring student-athletes’ academic progress and growth as a person. Individual workouts, conditioning, and strength training with team members. Competition day meal planning and organization. Assisting head coach in all phases of student-athlete mentoring and evaluation Other administrative duties as assigned. Competencies Ability to multi-task in a fast-paced environment Ability to work independently Must be able to work as a member of a team Detailed-oriented Goal-oriented Must be able to build relationships with prospective student-athletes and families, faculty and staff, community members, and external vendors Excellent communication and follow-up skills Must demonstrate entrepreneurial thinking Innovation and creativity Ability to maintain confidential information and files Supervisory Responsibility This position will not directly supervise staff, but it will have responsibility for such when it comes to student assistants and/or managers. Work Environment Normal office environment in addition to non-traditional environment that includes gymnasiums, weight room, locker room, and outdoor venues. Coach will be outdoors frequently, particularly during the winter season, at the Beech Mountain Ski Resort leading team workouts. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work This is a Part-time, 12-month position. Days and hours of work will vary. Typical work schedule will be Monday through Friday from 9:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m. Frequent evening and weekend work is required for recruitment and competition events. Travel Extensive day and overnight travel is required as needed. Must possess a valid state-issued driver’s license and a clean driving record. Additional Eligibility Qualifications Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Previous coaching or ski experience at the high school or college level Excellent written and oral communication, well-developed presentation skills, and outstanding customer and quality service skills Competency with Microsoft Office applications and social media marketing platforms Ability to build relationships with student-athletes and families Knowledge of USCSA and NCAA Division II rules and regulations Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in a related field L100 certification through USCSA Experience with Slate or another CRM Certifications: CPR , AED , and First Aid Physical Demands Coach should be actively skiing and in good condition to participate on the slopes for practices and competitions. The employee must occasionally climb, balance, stoop, kneel, crouch or crawl, and use tools. The employee must frequently lift or move up to 20 pounds and occasionally lift or move up to 50 pounds. Specific vision abilities required by this job include close vision, distance vision, color vision, peripheral vision, depth perception and ability to adjust focus Posting Detail Information Posting Number S135P Number of Vacancies 1 Job Open Date Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://leesmcrae.peopleadmin.com/postings/570 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Transcripts Letter of Recommendation Curriculum Vitae Media File Portfolio Office of Human Resources 191 Main Street Banner Elk, NC 28604 rectore@lmc.edu 828.898.8926 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://leesmcrae.peopleadmin.com/postings/569": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Advancement Operations",
      "description": "Lees-McRae College Portal | Assistant Director of Advancement Operations Skip to Main Content Career Opportunities Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Director of Advancement Operations Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Assistant Director of Advancement Operations Department MNC Job Description Position Title: Assistant Director of Advancement Operations Department: Advancement Operations/Institutional Advancement Reports To: Associate Director of Advancement Operations Lees-McRae is a small, four-year, liberal arts college serving Appalachia and the Southeastern United States. The College is located in the town of Banner Elk in the scenic Blue Ridge Mountains of northwestern North Carolina. Banner Elk is nestled between two popular ski areas and is within a short drive of the Blue Ridge Parkway, and the Appalachian Trail. The area is popular to outdoor enthusiasts: skiing, cycling, hiking, climbing and fly fishing are among the many attractions. The college also owns and maintains the Elk Valley Preserve and Field Station and the May Wildlife Rehabilitation Center. Please visit our website at www.lmc.edu. Benefits Lees-McRae College offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes Highmark Blue Cross/Blue Shield medical plans with wellness incentives, Aetna dental coverage with orthodontia for children, and a voluntary vision plan for all employees. Life and long-term disability insurance are employer-paid, with optional voluntary life coverage available. Employees can take advantage of flexible spending accounts, a retirement plan with up to 5% employer match after one year, and generous paid time off including vacation, sick, personal, holiday, and college-closed days. Tuition waiver benefits are available for employees and dependents, along with access to a national tuition exchange program. Additional perks include free monthly dining, discounted meal plans, and required direct deposit for payroll. Job Summary/Objective The Assistant Director of Advancement Operations provides strategic leadership and operational execution for the College’s advancement information infrastructure, CRM , data management, reporting, analytics, and technology systems. The position ensures that accurate, secure, accessible, and actionable constituent information is available to support fundraising, alumni relations, stewardship, communications, campaign management, and institutional decision-making. The Director serves as the primary operational and technical resource for Institutional Advancement and works collaboratively across the College to establish efficient systems, processes, standards, and integrations. The position also works in support of the broader needs of Advancement and Alumni Relations. Essential Functions Provides turnkey management and frontline accountability of the College’s advancement data and digital tools/services/ CRM to ensure their accuracy, functionality, ready accessibility, and evolution with modern practices. Investigates and leads best practices in data strategy, data management and protection, data collection, and data hygiene with an eye to both granular and systems-approach. Identifies and builds efficient systems, protocols, and daily practices for Advancement and data users across campus. Creates and maintains, in collaboration with other divisions, consistent data governance and procedures for entering, updating, documenting, and retrieving advancement information. Serves as a central operational resource for the Office of Institutional Advancement, the President’s Office, and other offices requiring constituents’ data. Develops and operationalizes proactive quality control procedures, auditing, and testing environments. Identifies and deploys various methods of statistical analysis and data visualization/presentation for effective communications about fundraising and alumni relations. Ensures that accurate, timely, and complete information about all constituents is maintained and readily available to support fundraising, alumni engagement, stewardship, communications, and institutional decision-making. Serves as lead in data maintenance and hygiene. Serves as the lead support for CRM data mapping and migration; anticipates and troubleshoots both transitional issues and concerns and future utilization impact. Ensures data safety protocols are in place and redundancy is established. Oversees the day-to-day functions that involve the Advancement database, including, but not limited to, maintaining or producing constituent records, gift and pledge records, biographical and relationship information, prospect assignments, fundraiser portfolios, moves management, contact reports, campaign data, reporting, screenings and prospect identification, heatmaps, fundraising reports and dashboards, lists for management and communications, statistical visualization, and seamless data transfer across various college software and applications. Cross-trains and maintains knowledge of gift recording, receipting, and acknowledgement processes, partners, external services to serve as secondary accountability. Provides training and materials to assist in system navigation and usage. Supports general needs and activities of the Advancement and Alumni Relations programs, including events, communications, and projects. Competencies Technical acumen and adaptability Discretion and confidentiality Anticipatory thinking Deep command of details Written and verbal communication proficiency Effective time management Problem solving/analysis Customer service and teamwork orientation Conscientious and dependable Supervisory Responsibility This position may oversee student workers, interns, or other staff as required. Work Environment Day to day work will typically occur in the offices of the division, but may sometimes require a presence across campus for meetings, projects, and activities. On occasion, work may be required in other locations and environments. Position Type/Expected Hours of Work This is a full-time, exempt position. Days and hours of work are Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. for daily operations. Night and weekend work is also required as needed to complete high priority projects, support events, or assist with college activities. Travel This position may require up to 20% travel, including long distance and overnight requirements, on a periodic basis. Required Qualifications Associates or Bachelor’s degree in computer science, information systems, data analytics, business administration, nonprofit management, higher education administration, or a related field; or an equivalent combination of education and relevant experience. At least 3-5 years of progressively responsible experience in one or more of the following fields: CRM /database administration, data management, institutional research, business intelligence, project management, advancement services, fundraising operations, or a related field. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to translate complex intelligence into clear information for non-technical users. Technical fluency with Microsoft Suite products, AI. Strong project management skills. Ability to manage competing priorities and work independently. Understanding of or willingness to learn advancement ethics, confidentiality, and appropriate use of donor Preferred Qualifications Experience with Ellucian Colleague/Enterprise, Salesforce, Blackbaud/Raiser’s Edge, or comparable advancement/ CRM platforms. Advanced knowledge of advancement CRM architecture and functionality. Experience with and ability to lead CRM migration, data hygiene and collection, data integration, reporting, analytics and business intelligence. Understanding of data ownership, permissions, security, retention, and privacy. Understanding of data flow and integrations among CRM , student/parent databases, finance, email and mass communication tools, payment processing and merchant accounts, and other institutional systems. Ability to work with vendors and IT personnel on APIs, imports/exports, data mapping, and integrations. Ability to document, redesign, and improve business processes. Experience working in a small college or university environment. High level of discretion when handling confidential constituent and financial information. Strong quantitative and analytical skills. Experience supporting a fundraising comprehensive or major campaign. Understanding of the fundraising lifecycle Knowledge of annual giving, major gifts, planned /deferred giving, campaigns, stewardship, alumni relations, events, research and prospect management. Physical Demands Must type proficiently and use a computer throughout day Must be able to lift up to 25 pounds Must sit for extended periods Must be able to travel independently Posting Detail Information Posting Number S134P Number of Vacancies 1 Job Open Date Special Instructions to Applicants Quick Link for Internal Postings https://leesmcrae.peopleadmin.com/postings/567 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Optional Documents Transcripts Letter of Recommendation Curriculum Vitae Media File Portfolio Office of Human Resources 191 Main Street Banner Elk, NC 28604 rectore@lmc.edu 828.898.8926 To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
